---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Estimator from '../components/Estimator.astro';
import models from '../data/models.json';
---
<Layout title="AICost Matrix — Explainable AI API Cost Calculator" description="Budget text API calls with separate cache reads, cache writes, output and extra calls. Source-linked reference prices and a local usage checker." canonical="https://aicost.apexcraftweb.com/">
 <section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">AI costs, with the assumptions visible</p><h1>From API tokens<br/>to a feature budget.</h1><p class="intro">Plan calls, cache costs and retries. See the arithmetic behind each estimate, or check a small set of actual usage records locally.</p><div class="actions"><a class="primary" href="#calculator">Build a budget</a><a class="secondary" href="/usage">Check usage records →</a></div><p class="hint">3 checked Claude reference models · free to use · stored prices, not live quotes</p></div></section>
 <div class="wrap flow"><Estimator/>
 <section class="panel" id="prices"><p class="eyebrow">2 · Know the price basis</p><h2>Small coverage. Traceable prices.</h2><p>Direct Claude API, global routing, prompts up to 100,000 tokens. Amounts below are standard USD per million tokens. Batch prices are half of each displayed rate. We do not price other providers, higher prompt tiers or fast/priority modes in this version.</p>
 <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Reference snapshot · checked 2026-11-14</caption><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Input</th><th>Output</th><th>Cache read</th><th>Write · 5m</th><th>Write · 1h</th></tr></thead><tbody>{models.map(m=><tr><td><a href={`/model/${m.id}`}>{m.name}</a></td>{['input','output','cacheRead','cacheWrite5m','cacheWrite1h'].map(k=><td>${m.rates[k]}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
 <p><a href="/methodology">Sources, scope and update policy →</a></p></section>
 <section class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">3 · Reconcile the inputs first</p><h2>Why does the dashboard cost differ?</h2><p>Cached input can have different meanings across APIs and SDKs. The usage checker maps direct Anthropic Messages records to separate billing buckets, flags conflicting counts and blocks duplicate responses.</p><p><a href="/usage">Open the local usage checker →</a></p></section>
 <section class="panel"><h2>Before using the number</h2>
 <details open><summary>Is this my actual bill?</summary><p>No. It is an estimate of supported text token fees at the stored prices. Tools, media, tax, credits, negotiated rates, regional premiums and your application infrastructure are excluded. Compare with a provider bill only after aligning scope, dates and currency.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Can I assume a cache hit rate?</summary><p>Use measured cache reads and writes where possible. Cache eligibility, minimum lengths and expiration vary. Writing a cache has a cost; a cheaper read rate is not a promise of whole-task savings.</p></details>
 <details><summary>What about reasoning, retries and Batch?</summary><p>Include billed thinking tokens in output, not as an extra copy. Enter retries as extra calls only once. Message Batches is asynchronous, and its discount does not mean a normal request is billed as Batch.</p></details>
 <details><summary>How do I check the arithmetic?</summary><p>Each bucket costs tokens × USD per million ÷ 1,000,000. A fictional price of $2 input and $10 output means 200 input + 300 output costs $0.0035 per call, or $35 for 10,000 calls. These example rates are not a current GPT-4o quote.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Does the cheapest model do the same work?</summary><p>Not necessarily. Tokenizers, quality, output length, latency and successful completion rates differ. Compare on the same real tasks before treating a token-price difference as a saving.</p></details>
 </section></div>
</Layout>
